The circumstances include: (SCC p. 286, para R/CR.A/1540/2013 JUDGMENT DATED: 08/08/2022 28) "(i) The High Court's decision is based on totally erroneous view of law by ignoring the settled legal position;
(ii) The High Court's conclusions are contrary to evidence and documents on record;
(iii) The entire approach of the High Court in dealing with the evidence was patently illegal leading to grave miscarriage of justice;
State Of Gujarat - Thro' H.L.Makwana, ... vs Parshottamchandra Rameshchandra ... on 8 August, 2022 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/153843708/
6

(iv) The High Court's judgment is manifestly unjust and unreasonable based on erroneous law and facts on the record of the case;
(v) This Court must always give proper weight and consideration to the findings of the High Court;
(vi) This Court would be extremely reluctant in interfering with a case when both the Sessions Court and the High Court have recorded an order of acquittal."

He also did not know about the details of panchnama of seizure;
iii) the Food Inspector (PW-1) has also admitted in his cross- examination that Notice in Form-VI, which was required to be given to the owner of the shop i.e.
Rameshbhai (accused No. 2) as per rules, was not given to him;
iv) in para 32 of the impugned judgment and order, the learned trial  R/CR.A/1540/2013 JUDGMENT DATED: 08/08/2022 Judge has observed that the sample in question was taken from the Ghee, which was seized by the police and kept without any seal.

Besides, it is not proved that the said Ghee, which was seized by the State Of Gujarat - Thro' H.L.Makwana, ... vs Parshottamchandra Rameshchandra ... on 8 August, 2022 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/153843708/
10 police, was meant for the purpose of selling;
v) PW-2 Mulubhai Bhikhabhai, Exh. 74, who is the panch witness, has not supported the case of the prosecution and declared hostile;
vi) there appears breach of Rule 14 of the Rules.
vii) the standard of proof in criminal cases is beyond reasonable doubt.
